==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|NL.|hidrōsis}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἱδρώς||sweat}} + {{m|la|-sis}}; also {{glossary|synchrony|synchronically}} held to end in the suffix {{m|en|-osis}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|hidroses}}

# {{senseid|en|sweating, noun, literally}} {{lb|en|physiology|medicine}} The formation and excretion of [[sweat]].
#: {{syn|en|sweating#Noun|perspiration<id:sweating, noun, literally>|;|q3=in medical usage|diaphoresis<id:sweating, noun, literally>|sudation|sudoresis}}
#: {{ant|en|adiaphoresis|anhidrosis|ischidrosis}}
#: {{hypo|en|q=excessive|hyperhidrosis|;|q2=insufficient|hypohidrosis}}
## {{senseid|en|excessive sweating, noun, literally}} {{lb|en|physiology|medicine|sometimes|more particularly}} Excessive [[sweating]]; excessive [[perspiration]] (more than would be expected in response to a given stimulus; especially when [[profuse]] as a [[symptom]] of [[disease]] or a [[side effect]] of a [[drug]]).
##: {{syn|en|hyperhidrosis|diaphoresis<id:excessive sweating, noun, literally>}}<!--"hidrosis" is a member of a smallish class of words (either adjectives or nouns) where "X" not only has a sense that is hypernymous to "hyper-X" but also has another sense that is synonymous with "hyper-X" (via polysemic imprecision); most such [[autohyponym]]ous pairs are "X-emia and hyper-X-emia" or "X-emic and hyper-X-emic" pairs, such as [[glycemia]] and [[hyperglycemia]], [[chloremia]]/-ic and [[hyperchloremia]]/-ic, and so on-->
##: {{ant|en|hypohidrosis}}

